Licence of the embedding model shipped in this image
====================================================

Model:     intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
Origin:    https://huggingface.co/intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
Revision:  614241f622f53c4eeff9890bdc4f31cfecc418b3
Read on:   2026-09-04

Licence:   MIT

Where that statement comes from, stated plainly because it matters here. The
upstream repository ships no LICENSE file of its own. The licence is declared in
the metadata of the model card and nowhere else: the HuggingFace API returns
`cardData.license = "mit"` for this repository and it carries the tag
`license:mit`. This file therefore reproduces the MIT text so that the licence
travels with the image, which is what is distributed.

For the same reason no copyright line is filled in below with a name: upstream
states the licence but names no copyright holder in a licence file, and an
attribution nobody wrote is worse than an honest gap. The repository is
maintained under the account `intfloat`, and the model is the multilingual E5
family described in "Multilingual E5 Text Embeddings: A Technical Report"
(arXiv:2402.05672).

What is distributed here is not the upstream file. The build takes the fp32
`onnx/model.onnx` of the revision above and quantises it to int8 itself, because
the int8 file upstream ships is AVX512-VNNI and therefore x86 only. The result
is a derived work of the model and travels under the same licence.

